      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.The original test has several understandability issues: unused imports, unused helper data methods not referenced by any test, and no explanation of what `ZERO` semantics mean. I'll write a cleaner version now.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed all unused imports (serialization, `Duration`, `LocalTime`, `DateTimeParseException`, `ParameterizedTest`, `MethodSource`, `EqualsTester`), removed the two unused data-provider methods (`data_valid` and `data_invalid`) that were never referenced by any test, and added a brief comment above `test_ZERO` explaining the intent of the `ZERO` constant and what the test verifies."
